-- examples/checks/agg-wfs-game.rofl — THE WELL-FOUNDED WORLD BELOW every
-- agg_<kind>_wfs world (docs/aggregates.md, "Well-founded worlds and ticks,
-- as built"). A position wins if some move reaches a position that does not
-- win. c and h win; d, g and i lose (no move, or every move reaches a win);
-- a, b, e and f are drawn: each wins only if the other does not, and the
-- alternating fixpoint leaves them `unknown(wg_win(X))`. Declared as the
-- world agg_wfs_game too, so both engines agree on what is fed.
semantics(well_founded).
edb(wg_move).
wg_move(a, b). wg_move(b, a).
wg_move(b, c). wg_move(c, d).
wg_move(e, f). wg_move(f, e).
wg_move(g, h). wg_move(h, i).
wg_win(X) :- wg_move(X, Y), not wg_win(Y).
